  "__comment": "One block cell of the portcullis lattice, TILED rather than stretched -- a grate is defined by its gaps and they must land on block boundaries. Bars and rails both sit on an 8px pitch, which makes the openings square like a real portcullis. Rails are deliberately at y 4 and 12 rather than 0 and 8: nothing then lands on the cell's bottom edge, so the foot of the gate ends in bar ends instead of a flat bar running across it. UVs are ignored -- the renderer projects the gate's texture across the whole grid.",
